description:
Write `int binarySearch(const std::vector<int>& sorted, int target)`. The vector is in ascending order. Return the index of `target`, or `-1` if it is not there.

Do not look at every element. Look at the middle one:

- if it is the target, you are done;
- if it is too small, the target can only be in the right half;
- if it is too big, only in the left half.

Each step throws away half of what is left, so a million elements need about 20 steps.

